# 98. Quarter-Long Skills Reinforced This Week

Unit 2 should continue reinforcing the larger Seminar III academic habits.

Students should practice:

## Reading Before Solving

Understand the problem before calculating.

## Selecting a Strategy

Do not assume every problem requires the same approach.

## Showing Enough Work to Diagnose Errors

Students should record enough of their process that they or the teacher can identify where something went wrong.

## Checking

Do not treat the first calculated answer as automatically correct.

## Learning From Errors

Identify what happened and choose an appropriate response.

## Retrying

Use feedback to attempt the skill again.

